    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d364">

                <pb facs="0370" n="254" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg254"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 837.00/690a.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the American
                    Minister</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-06-05">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 5, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Cuban authorities having failed to take effective action for the protection
                    of American life and property the commandant at Guantánamo naval station has
                    been compelled to land four companies of marines. This action has been taken as
                    a measure of protection only and not for the purpose of putting down the
                    insurrection, which is clearly the duty of Cuba. Four large war vessels will
                    forthwith be sent from Key West to Guantánamo. It is hoped these measures will
                    at once awaken the Cuban Government to prompt and adequate discharge of its
                    responsibilities, and you will vigorously impress upon the President of Cuba
                    that a continued failure on the part of his Government adequately to protect
                    life and property will inevitably compel this Government to intervene in Cuba
                    under and in response to its treaty rights and obligations.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Knox</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
